  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: 'The gold funerary mask of Pharaoh Tutankhamun (18th Dynasty, c. 1323 BCE), discovered in tomb KV62 in the Valley of the Kings by Howard Carter in 1922.\n\nCrafted from over 10 kilograms of solid gold inlaid with lapis lazuli, turquoise, carnelian, and quartz. The nemes headdress bears the protective cobra (Wadjet) and vulture (Nekhbet), symbolizing sovereign divine authority over Upper and Lower Egypt in the afterlife.'


    A placeholder is displayed on this table.

    The
    final model and information will be added later.'
